            introduction: 'Retirement might seem distant, but time is the most powerful wealth-building advantage you have. In India, retirement planning is especially important since most people do not have social security. The key retirement savings vehicles are: EPF (Employees\' Provident Fund) — a mandatory deduction of 12% of basic salary matched by your employer, earning around 8-8.5% interest tax-free. PPF (Public Provident Fund) — a voluntary 15-year account where you can invest up to ₹1.5 lakh per year at ~7-8% interest, completely tax-free (EEE status). NPS (National Pension System) — a market-linked retirement account with equity and debt options, offering additional tax benefits under Section 80CCD(1B) up to ₹50,000. ALWAYS contribute enough to get the full employer EPF match — it is free money with tax-free returns. For young people, starting early is everything. If you start investing ₹5,000 per month in an equity mutual fund at age 25 earning 12% returns, you will have about ₹2.6 crore at age 60. Start at 35 instead, and you end up with only about ₹79 lakh. That 10-year delay costs you over ₹1.8 crore. The earlier you start, the more powerful compound growth becomes.',
