                correctAnswer: '300%',
                explanation: 'Markup = (selling price - cost) / cost × 100 = (₹600 - ₹150) / ₹150 × 100 = 300%. This is normal for restaurants — you are paying for preparation, service, ambiance, and rent, not just ingredients.',
                hint: 'Markup is calculated as profit divided by cost, not as a percentage of the selling price.',
